From 5d855bcb37e080deb50d6706bdc49739b78b2b72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] A paused turn's continuation refused during its
 start-up keeps an owner

The kickoff ignored _run_prompt_submit's False: when the update hold was re-taken while the continuation
waited for its agent build, admission refused it, _auto_continue_scheduled stayed set, the pause watcher had
already exited on "scheduled", and the chat sat paused until the backend exited (hub, 40-51 min).

- session_auto_continue: a refused submit releases the claim, logs "continuation of <key> never started",
  re-arms the in-place watcher for a core-update pause (10 s backoff) or backs off 30 s otherwise.
- prompt_turn: "tui prompt refused ... cause=admission|closing|not_started" closes every accepted prompt
  that never started.

Regression tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_update_pause_refused_kickoff.py, test_prompt_refused_logging.py
(self-heal defect gateway-833d39a686, t_01a1d34a46d7bd6b)

Proof: the 14 regression tests fail 10 on the tree without the fix and pass 14 with it; 20 tui_gateway
update-pause/auto-continue/prompt files pass 270; all 15 mutants of the added conditions are killed
(is False vs falsy, release, except-return, paused/closing/finalized rearm, backoff, watcher, log causes).
